.TH ls 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
ls \- list directory contents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ls
[\fB\-1Radfilortu\fR] [\fIfile\fR ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ls
lists each
.IR file ,
and the contents of each directory named.  With no arguments it lists
the current directory.
.PP
Output is sorted by name unless
.B \-t
or
.B \-f
says otherwise, and is written in columns when standard output is a
terminal and in a single column when it is not.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-1
One name per line.
.TP
.B \-a
Include names beginning with a dot.
.TP
.B \-d
List a directory itself rather than its contents.
.TP
.B \-f
Do not sort, and imply
.BR \-a .
.TP
.B \-i
Print the inode number in the first column.
.TP
.B \-l
Long format: mode, link count, owner, group, size, time and name.
.TP
.B \-o
Long format without the group.
.TP
.B \-r
Reverse the sort order.
.TP
.B \-R
Descend into subdirectories.
.TP
.B \-t
Sort by modification time, newest first.
.TP
.B \-u
Use the access time rather than the modification time, for sorting with
.B \-t
and for display with
.BR \-l .
.SH NOTES
.B ll
is a separate program, not an alias: it always gives a long listing and
takes no options.
.PP
There is no
.BR \-h ,
no
.B \-\-color
and no
.BR \-F .
Sizes are in bytes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ll (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR du (1)
